'''''Pilea nummulariifolia''''' is a [[perennial plant|perennial]] evergreen [[herbaceous plant]] commonly known as '''creeping charlie''' native to the Caribbean (including [[Florida]]<ref>{{cite web | url = https://plants.usda.gov/java/profile?symbol=PINU&mapType=nativity&photoID= | work = PLANTS | title = Pilea nummulariifolia (Sw.) Weddell }}</ref>) and northern South America.<ref>{{cite web | url = http://www.gardening.eu/plants/Perennial-Plants/Pilea-nummulariifolia/1801/ | title = Creeping charlie Pilea nummulariifolia }}</ref><ref>{{GRIN | accessdate = 29 January 2018}}</ref>  It can be grown indoors, for example in a hanging pot.<ref>{{cite encyclopedia | url = http://www.britannica.com/eb/topic-142453/Creeping-Charlie | title = Creeping Charlie, or Pilea nummulariifolia, or Swedish Ivy (Pilea nummulariifolia) | encyclopedia = Encyclopædia Britannica }}</ref><ref>[http://ag.arizona.edu/pubs/garden/mg/indoor/baskets.html INDOOR PLANTS: PLANT LISTS] {{Webarchive|url=https://web.archive.org/web/20160510041412/http://ag.arizona.edu/pubs/garden/mg/indoor/baskets.html |date=2016-05-10 }}, ''Arizona Master Gardener Manual''</ref>

